---
name: ship
description: {{ ("Ship the current changes in " ~ a.name ~ ": run checks, review, then commit, push and open a PR after the user confirms") | tojson }}
disable-model-invocation: true
---

Ship the current changes. Stop and report at the first failure.

1. Run `git status` and `git diff HEAD`. If there are no changes, say so and stop. If you're on the default branch, propose a branch name and ask before creating it.
{% if a.lint_cmd %}
2. Lint: `{{ a.lint_cmd }}`
{% else %}
2. Lint: no lint command is configured in `AGENTS.md`; skip and say so.
{% endif %}
{% if a.test_cmd %}
3. Test: `{{ a.test_cmd }}`
{% else %}
3. Test: no test command is configured in `AGENTS.md`; ask the user how to verify before going further.
{% endif %}
4. Review the diff for bugs and leftover debug code. If the change affects anything people see or use, run the `humane-design-reviewer` subagent{% if "code-reviewer" in a.agents %}, and run the `code-reviewer` subagent on larger changes{% endif %}.
5. Draft a commit message: a short summary line, then why the change was made.
6. Show the user the checks you ran, the review findings and the message. **Wait for their go-ahead** before you commit, push or open a PR.
7. Commit, push, and open a pull request (`gh pr create` if the GitHub CLI is installed). Reply with the PR link.
